# Maximum Overdrive targets "target creature", so an opponent's creature is a legal target too (CR 115.1): Bot1 puts the
# counter on Bot2's Ornithopter (0/2), making it 1/3 with deathtouch and indestructible until end of turn. Bot1's Bolt (3
# damage) is lethal damage to a 1/3 but indestructible keeps it (CR 702.12b). The counter is Bot2's permanent's, not Bot1's.
# The Spell cannot target a noncreature permanent (a Mox): refused beside the creature it allows.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Jet
Mox Ruby
Lightning Bolt
Maximum Overdrive
Mountain
Island x15

[Bot2 Deck]
Ornithopter
Island x19

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
! Bot1.Hand.Maximum Overdrive.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet)
Bot1.Hand.Maximum Overdrive.Cast(Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Mana = 
? Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Power = 1
? Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Toughness = 3
? Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Keywords = Deathtouch; Flying; Indestructible
? Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Counters.PlusOnePlusOne = 1
Bot1.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Damage = 3
[T4 Bot2.Main1]
? Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Keywords = Flying
? Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Power = 1
? Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Toughness = 3

[Expect]
Turn = 4
Bot2.Battlefield = Ornithopter
Bot1.Graveyard = Lightning Bolt; Maximum Overdrive
